# Keep the working tree LF on every platform. Without this a Windows clone
# (core.autocrlf=true by default) lands CRLF in every file, and `prettier
# --check .` then fails on all of them at once -- Prettier normalises to LF
# and has no idea the checkout did it. It also keeps the SQL and shell
# scripts that get mounted into containers readable to the tools inside.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
